OL,3,GNEWSAMum wants grassroots football to
OL,4,Abe more inclusive
OL,5,
OL,6,FA parent and GP is pushing for
OL,7,Fgrassroots football to be more
OL,8,Finclusive after her son, who has
OL,9,Fdyspraxia, felt forced out of his club
OL,10,Ffor being a "weaker player".
OL,12,FMillie has said her eight-year-old son
OL,13,FArthur's condition affects his balance,
OL,14,Fco-ordination and processing, and he
OL,15,Fwas given less game time than his peers
OL,16,Funtil he stopped playing.
OL,18,FShe said she would like all children to
OL,19,Fbe able to "go and play at their local
OL,20,Fteam, play alongside their friends, and
OL,21,Ffor it to be genuinely inclusive".
OL,23,APub: 26-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
